<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<!--
    "Northbeam Dispatch" — home screen of a fictional US freight carrier
    (Northbeam Freight, Columbus OH). This is the heavy screen the
    "Open a screen" benchmark opens.

    DispatchHomeXamlC.xaml and DispatchHomeXamlC.xaml are byte-identical
    except for x:Class; the only variable is the Inflator metadata in the
    csproj. Edit THIS file, then regenerate the twin:
      sed 's/DispatchHomeXamlC/DispatchHomeXamlC/' DispatchHomeSourceGen.xaml > DispatchHomeXamlC.xaml

    Light palette (2026-11-04) so the screen reads as a white app against the
    video's dark background; same structure as the dark version that was
    measured, only colors changed.

    Rules that keep the number honest:
    - No page ResourceDictionary: colors are inline, so LazyRD (SourceGen only)
      can't sneak into the XamlC vs SourceGen comparison.
    - Nothing animates: the screen is static once drawn, so "first frame" is
      a clean end point.
    - It is a ContentView, not a page: the launcher swaps it in as its own
      content instead of navigating. Same work (inflate, attach, handlers,
      layout, draw) without Shell navigation in the number — and Shell
      pops hung on return in preview 5.
-->
<ContentView
    xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/dotnet/2021/maui"
    xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2009/xaml"
    xmlns:material="clr-namespace:HorusStudio.Maui.MaterialDesignControls;assembly=HorusStudio.Maui.MaterialDesignControls"
